---
description: SANAD native game engine rules (no HTML games)
alwaysApply: true
---

SANAD is a native C++23 + Vulkan game engine. A game is a `.nfproj` project with
`.nfscene` text scenes and Lua gameplay, built by the `nf` CLI.

- **Never** create HTML/CSS/JavaScript, `index.html`, `package.json`, Electron, a
  web server, or a Unity/Godot/Unreal project when asked to make a game.
- Create projects with `nf new Games\<Name> --template ThirdPerson`.
- Edit `Content/Scenes/*.nfscene` and `Content/Scripts/*.lua`.
- Verify with `nf run --project <file> --frames 120 --headless --validation`;
  acceptance is exit code 0 and `Validation errors: 0`.
- Read `AGENTS.md` and `Docs/AI_Game_Guide.md` before starting.
- Do not edit `Engine/` for a gameplay task.
